{
  "id": "COMPOUND:21112 - PROTEIN:5826",
  "verbalization": "Guvacine Hydrochloride is implicated in the pathogenesis of SMMC-7721, a human liver cancer cell line, through a series of mechanistic links. The drug is directly linked to VMRC-LCP, which is a target of Ginsenoside R10, a bioactive compound found in plant sources. Ginsenoside R10, in turn, targets SMMC-7721, suggesting a potential role in cancer suppression. The evidence suggests that Guvacine Hydrochloride may act through a pathway involving Ginsenoside R10, which could modulate cellular processes in SMMC-7721 cells. The observed scores indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, supported by the sequential targeting of VMRC-LCP and Ginsenoside R10 to SMMC-7721. The mechanism appears to involve the inhibition of a target protein, possibly through a complex involving plant-derived compounds. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Guvacine Hydrochloride to exert its effects via a multi-step process involving plant-derived metabolites, which may contribute to its therapeutic potential against SMMC-7721.",
